bout unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in the present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Perfect Modals: Could Have", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "To express uncertainty about past events, use the Perfect modal phrase <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">could have</span></span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">could have</span></span> + past participle to:<br/>  <ul><li>explain that you were able to do something in the past, but didn't. <br/> For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have gone</span> to their party, but I didn't want to.</span></li>  <li>talk about a suggestion that was not taken<br/>  For example:<br/>   <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\"> could have asked</span> your teacher to give you a different assignment.</span>  <br/> <li>discuss an action that nearly happened, but didn't.<br/>  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Watch out! That car <span class=\"strong\">could have killed</span> you!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Alex wondered how he and Jennifer could have managed to stay happily married all these years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He decided that his wife could have arrived at the bank exactly on time and then left.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You could have waited a little longer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You couldn't have been there.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Non-Finite Clauses with -<span class=\"italic\">ing</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you think of a clause, you think of it having its own subject and verb. There are cases, however, when the clause does not contain a main verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "These are examples of non-defining clauses and the two clauses have the same subject:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Actions happening at the same time<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Waving their hands and cheering</span>, the guests congratulated the young couple.  </span></li><br/> <li>One action happening before another <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Opening the envelope</span>, she found that it contained a check for $1,000.  </span><br/><br/> You often explain the <span class=\"strong\">reason for something happening</span> with this type of clause.  <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Realizing there was no one at home</span>, I left the package on the porch.  </span><br/><br/> Both these types of sentence might begin with <span class=\"italic\">on</span> or <span class=\"italic\">upon</span>: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">On opening the envelope ... Upon realizing ...  </span></li><br/>  <li>An event which is the result of another event <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I didn't get lost, <span class=\"strong\">having remembered to bring a map</span>. </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Being a prompt and meticulous person, Jennifer was always very specific about any arrangements she made.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Realizing that Alex was likely to forget, Jennifer reminded him to come on time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Smiling to himself, Alex wondered how he and Jennifer could have managed to stay happily married all these years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Feeling very annoyed, Alex went straight home. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Upon arriving home, Alex wasn't surprised to see that Jennifer had already arrived. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "prompt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "done without delay; immediate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Being a prompt and meticulous person, Jennifer was always very specific about any arrangements she made. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about personalities and relationships.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meticulous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "showing great attention to detail; very careful and precise", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Being a prompt and meticulous person, Jennifer was always very specific about any arrangements she made. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "easy-going", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relaxed and tolerant ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Her husband Alex, on the other hand, was an easy-going fellow, who was usually late.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reproach", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to express disapproval or disappointment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Before Jennifer could say a word, Alex reproached her, with annoyance in his voice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "annoyance", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the feeling or state of being annoyed; irritation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Before Jennifer could say a word, Alex reproached her, with annoyance in his voice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in my book", "type": "name"}, {"content": " in my opinion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In my book, five minutes late isn't late.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "calmly", "type": "name"}, {"content": " in a relaxed way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: \"Alex,\" Jennifer said calmly, \"you were there at the right time\u201d. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Interview a partner about the past. Find out where your partner went to school and worked.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write ten sentences about your partner's past based on your interview.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Rewrite each sentence using \u201cCould have\u201d (e.g. He could have traveled to Paris, but he went to university instead.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your new sentences to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I interview a partner about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I speculate about the past using \u201cCould have\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my ideas with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}